  "source": "steps D2 and D3 designs (#73): D2 sections 3.1 and 3.2, D3 sections 3.2 and 3.3, 2026-11-24; synthetic values. `content` is the JSON of a kind 1 message the session's bot writes; `reads` is what the app takes from it: for `say` `footer` the line under the reply (`duration`, null when `markdown` is empty), the session's line for the panel's header (`session`, null when absent or not a string) and the account's values (`usage`: `at`, the two windows and `cost`, the session's estimated cost in US dollars, which the bot writes only for an account with no plan; null when absent or not of this shape); for `say` `title` the thread's name (`title`, null when empty). `usageLines` are the account's line, under a thread's composer (`place` `composer`) and in Settings, Bots (`place` `bots`), or null for no line: `profileRead` whether the bot's profile has been read, `plan` its plan, `windows` the bot's newest `usage` that carries a window, `cost` the thread's own newest `usage` that carries a cost (composer only), `apiSeen` whether any `usage` of that bot carried a cost, `now` epoch milliseconds; `<until>` is the core's `formatUntil` of `resetsAt - now`, a reset already passed leaves out its `↻`, and `as of HH:mm` in `timeZone` follows when the `at` of the usage the line draws is more than 10 minutes before `now`",
